in one of the sessions.

00:04:27.337 --> 00:04:29.860
I'm like, oh, you thought
that was controversial,

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:31.235
wait til you see what's coming, man.

00:04:31.235 --> 00:04:34.001
Wait til my session (laughs).

00:04:34.001 --> 00:04:35.258
We're going to bring it.

00:04:35.258 --> 00:04:37.495
Anyway, back to the hotel.

00:04:37.495 --> 00:04:40.328
(uplifting music)

00:04:50.864 --> 00:04:55.031
So it's four o'clock, I have
to be at the stage at 4:30

00:04:56.238 --> 00:04:58.544
to practice, to get set
up, mic'd up, all that.

00:04:58.544 --> 00:05:01.725
And then at 5:30 I go live,
I'm super pumped about that.

00:05:01.725 --> 00:05:03.914
Did not sleep very well at all.

00:05:03.914 --> 00:05:07.197
I think the combination of
the coffee being in my system,

00:05:07.197 --> 00:05:08.197
(phone rings)

00:05:08.197 --> 00:05:10.503
oh, they're calling me, wake up call.

00:05:10.503 --> 00:05:11.336
Hello?

00:05:13.004 --> 00:05:17.171
Combination of the coffee,
that large Starbucks coffee,

00:05:18.397 --> 00:05:22.564
plus being worried about
the alarms not going off,

00:05:23.458 --> 00:05:25.699
so that one actually just
worked, you heard it.

00:05:25.699 --> 00:05:27.476
I set one on my phone and I set one for

00:05:27.476 --> 00:05:29.476
the phone that was here.

00:05:30.402 --> 00:05:32.573
I'm always worried that the
alarm is not going to go off,

00:05:32.573 --> 00:05:34.947
and so it prevents me from sleeping.

00:05:34.947 --> 00:05:37.240
And also just thinking
about the presentation.

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:39.556
And I always put a lot
of pressure on myself

00:05:39.556 --> 00:05:43.596
to do a great job because
I'm spending time away.

00:05:43.596 --> 00:05:46.395
It's four days away, pretty much.

00:05:46.395 --> 00:05:48.107
Three days away?

00:05:48.107 --> 00:05:50.302
Monday, Tuesday,
Wednesday, three days away.

00:05:50.302 --> 00:05:52.385
Still a lot of time away.

00:05:53.313 --> 00:05:55.333
And so this has to work, you know.

00:05:55.333 --> 00:05:56.519
Not just because I'm getting paid,

00:05:56.519 --> 00:05:59.218
but I'm missing out on other
opportunities to help people,

00:05:59.218 --> 00:06:01.029
so this has to be great.

00:06:01.029 --> 00:06:03.990
And so those combination of things made it

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:06.362
not conducive to sleeping.

00:06:06.362 --> 00:06:08.349
But it's okay, and I'm
really trying to think of

00:06:08.349 --> 00:06:10.845
anytime I complain to
see the positive side.

00:06:10.845 --> 00:06:13.235
We talked about that
earlier on in this vlog.

00:06:13.235 --> 00:06:15.082
So I'm really grateful
that I have a hotel room

00:06:15.082 --> 00:06:17.631
that's right across the street
from the conference center

00:06:17.631 --> 00:06:19.506
that I can easily come back to.

00:06:19.506 --> 00:06:22.879
I'm grateful that I have a
nice, soft bed to sleep in,

00:06:22.879 --> 00:06:27.192
at least relax in and not be
forced to be out and about

00:06:27.192 --> 00:06:29.253
losing more energy.

00:06:29.253 --> 00:06:31.028
I heard a baby cry for a little bit

00:06:31.028 --> 00:06:33.572
and so I'm really grateful
for that baby not freaking out

00:06:33.572 --> 00:06:34.895
because I've been in hotel rooms

00:06:34.895 --> 00:06:37.839
where the baby cries all
night and that sucks.

00:06:37.839 --> 00:06:39.085
And it's pretty clean air.

00:06:39.085 --> 00:06:41.327
There's a lot of smoking
in general in Paris

00:06:41.327 --> 00:06:43.104
and I get allergic to smoking

00:06:43.104 --> 00:06:44.757
so it's great that it's so clean.

00:06:44.757 --> 00:06:46.674
So that's the positive.

00:06:47.618 --> 00:06:51.620
I had a shower, I changed,
new shirt, look at that.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:55.021
Special new shirt, this
is the performance shirt.

00:06:55.021 --> 00:06:59.212
And I'm pumped, I'm excited
and ready to go speak

00:06:59.212 --> 00:07:01.105
and I'm going to take you guys with me.

00:07:01.105 --> 00:07:02.363
All right, I'm here.

00:07:02.363 --> 00:07:03.745
It's almost showtime.

00:07:03.745 --> 00:07:05.180
We're getting set up.

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:07.943
There it is a Club Talentsoft in the back.

00:07:07.943 --> 00:07:11.972
Here's the room again, going
to be filled with people.

00:07:11.972 --> 00:07:12.997
I'm pumped.

00:07:12.997 --> 00:07:16.291
- Let's call our last speaker
today, last but not least,

00:07:16.291 --> 00:07:19.478
he is a successful entrepreneur
on a mission to help

00:07:19.478 --> 00:07:22.605
one million entrepreneurs,
just that, right.

00:07:22.605 --> 00:07:25.283
He is the author of this
absolutely great book,

00:07:25.283 --> 00:07:29.290
find Your One Word, and
is a rockstar on YouTube

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:32.270
with more than 700,000 subscribers,

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:33.427
ladies and gentlemen,

00:07:33.427 --> 00:07:37.427
please give a warm welcome
to Evan Carmichael!

00:07:37.427 --> 00:07:40.177
(audience claps)

00:07:41.409 --> 00:07:43.627
- I love being in a room full of leaders.

00:07:43.627 --> 00:07:46.169
I love being in a room full of people

00:07:46.169 --> 00:07:49.536
who want to be inspired,
who come to learn,

00:07:49.536 --> 00:07:51.091
who want to improve themselves,

00:07:51.091 --> 00:07:53.303
who want to take the
knowledge that they took here

00:07:53.303 --> 00:07:54.986
and apply it to their business.

00:07:54.986 --> 00:07:57.228
And most importantly, I
love being with people

00:07:57.228 --> 00:07:59.165
who want to take action,

00:07:59.165 --> 00:08:01.349
because that's what we do as leaders.

00:08:01.349 --> 00:08:03.079
Everybody stand up, just quickly.

00:08:03.079 --> 00:08:05.243
Quick exercise, everybody stand up.

00:08:05.243 --> 00:08:06.873
Get the house lights up a little bit.

00:08:06.873 --> 00:08:08.401
I didn't prep these guys for it.

00:08:08.401 --> 00:08:09.696
Everybody stand up.

00:08:09.696 --> 00:08:11.739
I want you to put your hands up like this.

00:08:11.739 --> 00:08:13.615
Everybody put your hands up like this.

00:08:13.615 --> 00:08:15.449
Here we go, all right.

00:08:15.449 --> 00:08:17.551
When I count to three,
what we're going to do

00:08:17.551 --> 00:08:20.349
is we're going to turn
to the person next to us,

00:08:20.349 --> 00:08:21.690
we're going to give them a high ten,

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:23.569
and we're going to say,
you're a leader baby!

00:08:23.569 --> 00:08:25.740
(audience laughs)

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:27.245
Don't laugh, I'm serious!

00:08:27.245 --> 00:08:28.532
Okay, you're a leader baby!

00:08:28.532 --> 00:08:30.489
One, two, three.

00:08:30.489 --> 00:08:32.731
- [Audience] You're a leader baby!

00:08:32.731 --> 00:08:34.377
- Other side, other side!

00:08:34.377 --> 00:08:35.649
You're a leader baby!

00:08:35.649 --> 00:08:37.483
- [Audience] You're a leader baby!

00:08:37.483 --> 00:08:40.066
(upbeat music)

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:42.997
- Crushed the speech.

00:08:42.997 --> 00:08:44.614
They're now celebrating with a giant ball,

00:08:44.614 --> 00:08:46.326
